problems.problem:
Calculate the ratio of the mean densities of the Earth and the Sun ($\rho_E/\rho_S$), using only the following data:

(a) the angular diameter of the Sun as observed from the Earth ($\theta_S = 30'$);

(b) the acceleration of gravity at the surface of the Earth ($g = 9.81\ \mathrm{m/s^2}$);

(c) the length of the terrestrial year (365.5 days);

(d) the information that "a latitude of $\varphi = 1^\circ$ on the surface of the Earth corresponds to a length of 111 km".
